# admri

Preprocessing of structural MRI (T1-weighted) in **BIDS** format to build 2D
inputs for deep learning models, applied to Alzheimer's disease (ADNI).

This repository restructures the code of the Master's Thesis
*Exploring the use of Deep Learning to identify Early Alzheimer's Disease
patterns using MRI* (Irene Cuéllar Vázquez, Universitat de Barcelona, 2026;
original code: [irene-cuellar/TFM_Irene_Cuellar](https://github.com/irene-cuellar/TFM_Irene_Cuellar))
into a reusable package. The model part will be added later.

## Pipeline

```
T1w (BIDS) ──► skull stripping (HD-BET) ──► registration to MNI152 1 mm (ANTs SyN)
                                                   │            └──► tissue maps (CSF/GM/WM) warped
                                                   ▼
                         slices / patches ──► resize 224 ──► Gaussian intensity normalisation ──► .npy
```

It runs in two independent steps:

| Step | What it does | How often |
|---|---|---|
| `anat` | anatomical preprocessing: skull stripping, registration, tissue maps (optional) | once per dataset (slow) |
| `slices` | slice/patch extraction, resize, normalisation | once per input configuration (fast) |

## Code

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `scripts/preprocess.py` | command line entry point (`--step anat`, `slices` or `all`) |
| `src/admri/common.py` | configuration (`DEFAULTS`, `load_config`), reading/writing images, running a step for many images |
| `src/admri/bids.py` | find the input images (pybids) and build BIDS derivative paths |
| `src/admri/anat.py` | step `anat`: skull stripping, registration, tissue maps |
| `src/admri/slices.py` | step `slices`: slices/patches, resize, normalisation, saving |

## Installation

```bash
git clone <this repo>
cd admri
pip install -e ".[dev]"            # add ",tissue_maps" for ANTsPy (needed to warp the tissue maps)
```

Skull stripping and registration need the group's preprocessing functions
(`fun_defs.py`) and HD-BET; their locations are set in the dataset config
(`group_tools`).

## Usage

1. Copy the example configs and edit the paths (the copies are ignored by git):

   ```bash
   cp configs/datasets/adni.example.yaml configs/datasets/adni.yaml
   cp configs/experiments/anat.example.yaml configs/experiments/anat.yaml
   cp configs/experiments/coronal_3slices.example.yaml configs/experiments/coronal_3slices.yaml
   ```

2. Anatomical preprocessing of all subjects (blocks with `--start/--end` can
   run in parallel). Each step (skull stripping, registration, tissue maps) is
   skipped for the subjects whose outputs already exist:

   ```bash
   python scripts/preprocess.py --config configs/experiments/anat.yaml --step anat
   ```

3. Build the 2D inputs of an experiment:

   ```bash
   python scripts/preprocess.py --config configs/experiments/coronal_3slices.yaml --step slices --n-jobs 8
   ```

   The output folder contains the images, `images.csv` (one row per image),
   `log.csv` (status of each subject) and `config_used.yaml`.

## Configuration

Configs are split in two files:

- **`configs/datasets/<name>.yaml`**: everything specific to a dataset (BIDS
  root, which subjects/sessions, which T1w to prefer, paths to the group tools,
  the template and the FAST segmentations). To use a new BIDS dataset, only a
  new file here is needed.
- **`configs/experiments/<name>.yaml`**: processing choices (view, number of
  slices, resize, normalisation, output format). Points to a dataset config.

The available inputs of the original work have an example each:
`coronal_3slices`, `coronal_20slices`, `axial_3slices`, `coronal_patches`,
`tissue_maps`. Set `slices.legacy_uint8: true` to reproduce the 8-bit rounding
of the original PNG-based pipeline exactly.

## Outputs (BIDS derivatives)

```
derivatives/admri/
├── dataset_description.json
├── sub-<id>/ses-<id>/anat/
│   ├── sub-<id>_ses-<id>[_run-<n>]_desc-brain_T1w.nii.gz
│   ├── sub-<id>_ses-<id>[_run-<n>]_space-MNI152NLin6Asym_desc-brain_T1w.nii.gz
│   ├── sub-<id>_ses-<id>[_run-<n>]_from-T1w_to-MNI152NLin6Asym_desc-warp_xfm.nii.gz
│   ├── sub-<id>_ses-<id>[_run-<n>]_from-T1w_to-MNI152NLin6Asym_desc-affine_xfm.mat
│   └── sub-<id>_ses-<id>[_run-<n>]_space-MNI152NLin6Asym_label-GM_probseg.nii.gz
├── logs/  (anat_<start>-<end>.csv, anat_config_used_<start>-<end>.yaml)
└── slices/<experiment>/  (2D inputs, images.csv, log.csv, config_used.yaml)
```

## Data availability

ADNI data are subject to a data use agreement and are **not** included. The
`.gitignore` excludes images, CSV files and local configs.

## Tests

```bash
pytest
```

`tests/test_equivalence.py` checks that the new functions reproduce the
original pipeline on a synthetic volume.
